Ok.  Here is where I think arrows break in the code (dothrow.c):

int broken, chance;
		    chance = 3 + greatest_erosion(obj) - obj->spe;
		    if (chance > 1)
			broken = rn2(chance);
		    else
			broken = !rn2(4);
		    if (obj->blessed && !rnl(4))
			broken = 0;

I'm trying to figure out how to minimize chances of arrows breaking
(if that would be helpful).

It looks to me like obj->spe is the enchantment so if the arrows are
+2 and not rusted, etc. then enchanting over that doesn't help.  At +2
you have a 25% chance of an arrow breaking.  If it is blessed then you
have a lesser chance with your luck factored in.

this is from rnl() in rnd.c:

	if (Luck && rn2(50 - Luck)) {
	    i -= (x <= 15 && Luck >= -5 ? Luck/3 : Luck);
	    if (i < 0) i = 0;
	    else if (i >= x) i = x-1;
	}

I think Luck maxes out at 13 so with a luckstone and maxed out luck it
would appear that blessed arrows have a very small chance of being
broken.

I think it is 3/4*1/37 = about 2% with max luck of 13.

Let me know if my reasoning is faulty here.

